  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nI'd like an AI agent (Claude Code, or any MCP client) to program parts in CamCraft for me: open a model, set up stock and work offsets, add and tune operations, run the verifier, and post the G-code. Today that only works by clicking through the UI. `camcraft-cli` exists, but an agent has no structured way to see the job's state or to change it a step at a time.\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\nA Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, either built into the app or run as `camcraft-cli mcp` (stdio), with tools like:\n\n- **Job:** open or import a model (STEP, STL, OBJ), create or save a job, and inspect the job: setups, stock, WCS, tools, operations and their parameters.\n- **Setup:** set stock, work offsets, the machine and fixtures.\n- **Operations:** list the operation types and their parameter schemas, add, edit, reorder or delete an operation, pick its area (faces, edges, loops), and choose its tool.\n- **Verify and simulate:** run the verifier and return its findings (gouges, rest material, rapid and fixture collisions) as data, and take a screenshot or render of the simulation.\n- **Post:** pick a post processor and write the NC file, the setup sheet and the tool list.\n\nReplies should be structured (JSON) so an agent can check results, and every command should be undoable. If the app is already open, a live connection would let the user watch the agent work in the viewport. Refusals (anything the verifier can't prove safe) should come back as named errors the agent can act on.\n",
